<title>USA: Merrill, Ferris bids rejected on W.Va. deal.</title>
<headline>Merrill, Ferris bids rejected on W.Va. deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co and Ferris, Baker Watts Inc Tuesday said their bids on a $50 million West Virginia infrastructure general obligation bond sale were rejected. The winner remains to be determined, but it appears to be Smith Barney Inc at a 5.547 percent true interest cost.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
